    "content": "{\n  \"files\": [\n    {\n      \"content\": \"#include <stdio.h>\\n#include <stdlib.h>\\n#include <string.h>\\n#include <math.h>\\n#ifdef _OPENMP\\n#include <omp.h>\\n#endif\\n\\n#define N_ITER 10 // number of simulation iterations\\n#define DT 0.01f // time step\\n#define SOFTENING 1e-9f // to avoid zero divisors\\n\\n/*\\n * Each body holds coordinate positions (i.e., x, y, and z) and\\n * velocities (i.e., vx, vy, and vz).\\n */\\ntypedef struct { float x, y, z, vx, vy, vz; } Body;\\n\\n/*\\n * Compute the gravitational impact among all pairs of bodies in \\n * the system.\\n */\\nvoid body_force(Body *p, float dt, int n) {\\n  #pragma omp parallel for schedule(static,1)\\n  for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\\n    float fx = 0.0f; \\n    float fy = 0.0f; \\n    float fz = 0.0f;\\n\\n    for (int j = 0; j < n; j++) {\\n      float dx = p[j].x - p[i].x;\\n      float dy = p[j].y - p[i].y;\\n      float dz = p[j].z - p[i].z;\\n      float sqrd_dist = dx*dx + dy*dy + dz*dz + SOFTENING;\\n      float inv_dist = 1 / sqrt(sqrd_dist);\\n      float inv_dist3 = inv_dist * inv_dist * inv_dist;\\n\\n      fx += dx * inv_dist3; \\n      fy += dy * inv_dist3; \\n      fz += dz * inv_dist3;\\n    }\\n\\n    p[i].vx += dt*fx; \\n    p[i].vy += dt*fy; \\n    p[i].vz += dt*fz;\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n/*\\n * Read a binary dataset with initilized bodies.\\n */\\nBody* read_dataset(int *nbodies) {\\n  int b = fread(nbodies, sizeof(*nbodies), 1, stdin);\\n  if (b != 1) {\\n    fprintf(stderr,\\\"\\\\nError reading nbodie value\\\\n\\\");\\n    exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\\n  }\\n  Body *bodies = (Body *)malloc(*nbodies * sizeof(Body));\\n  b = fread(bodies, *nbodies * sizeof(Body), 1, stdin);\\n  if (b != 1) {\\n    fprintf(stderr,\\\"\\\\nError reading input values\\\\n\\\");\\n    exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\\n  }\\n\\n  return bodies;\\n}\\n\\n/*\\n * Write simulation results into a binary dataset.\\n */\\nvoid write_dataset(const int nbodies, Body *bodies) {\\n  int b = fwrite(bodies, nbodies * sizeof(Body), 1, stdout);\\n  if (b != 1) {\\n    fprintf(stderr,\\\"\\\\nError writing to output\\\\n\\\");\\n    exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nint main(int argc,char **argv) {\\n  int nbodies;\\n\\n  Body *bodies = read_dataset(&nbodies);\\n\\n  /*\\n   * At each simulation iteration, interbody forces are computed,\\n   * and bodies' positions are integrated.\\n   */\\n  for (int iter = 0; iter < N_ITER; iter++) {\\n    body_force(bodies, DT, nbodies);\\n\\n    #pragma omp parallel for schedule(static,1)\\n    for (int i = 0; i < nbodies; i++) {\\n      bodies[i].x += bodies[i].vx * DT;\\n      bodies[i].y += bodies[i].vy * DT;\\n      bodies[i].z += bodies[i].vz * DT;\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  write_dataset(nbodies, bodies);\\n\\n  free(bodies);\\n  \\n  exit(EXIT_SUCCESS);\\n}\\n\",\n      \"path\": \"src/nbody.c\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"hypothesis\": \"Using OpenMP static scheduling with chunk size 1 interleaves iterations across threads, reducing false sharing on per-body velocity/position updates while preserving deterministic accumulation order. This should outperform contiguous static chunks and approach the manual stride partitioning result without explicit thread management overhead.\",\n  \"notes\": \"This experiment tests whether OpenMP's runtime can match manual striding for this nbody kernel. The schedule(static,1) distributes body indices round-robin across threads, spacing writes to Body structs by at least one cache line (96 bytes apart), avoiding false sharing on velocity and position updates while keeping the inner j-loop sequential per body.\",\n  \"sources_kept\": [],\n  \"transformations\": [\n    \"Added OpenMP parallel-for pragmas with schedule(static,1) to the outer force loop in body_force\",\n    \"Added OpenMP parallel-for pragma with schedule(static,1) to the position integration loop in main\"\n  ]\n}",
